    40	| Strong consistency under S | **False already for unique scalar least squares** | Theorem 3: original ->0 a.s.; pooled limsup/liminf are +1/2 and -1/2 a.s. |
    41	| Triangular original designs, weak consistency | **False for p=4**, even when every original minimizer is consistent and every pooled selection is inconsistent | Theorem 5; not a solution of the nested question |
    42	| Literal “arbitrary measurable argmin selection” | False through an explicit artificial tie rule | Theorem 6; diagnostic only |
    43	
    44	The book's 2009 “no progress beyond LSE” statement must not be turned into “no later M-consistency results.” Wang–Hu [arXiv:1505.07178](https://arxiv.org/abs/1505.07178), published as [DOI 10.1007/s00184-015-0554-8](https://doi.org/10.1007/s00184-015-0554-8), gives a later strong-consistency sufficient theorem, not the desired implication from consistency alone. Exact source scope and access failures are in [sources/reading-notes.md](sources/reading-notes.md).
    45	
    46	## State of the art
    47	
    48	This is the strongest **directly checked** relevant theory found, not a claim to a globally exhaustive/latest bibliography.
    49	
    50	| Estimator/regime | Directly checked result | Primary source |
    51	|---|---|---|
    52	| LSE, fixed nested full-rank design, i.i.d. mean-zero errors with finite nonzero variance | Weak consistency iff lambda_min(S_n)->infinity | [Drygas (1976), Theorem 3.1](https://doi.org/10.1007/BF00535679); complete PDF saved |
    53	| LSE, independent mean-zero errors with uniformly bounded second moments | S_n^(-1)->0 implies strong consistency for the nested design | [Lai–Robbins–Wei (1978), Theorem 1, p. 3034](https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.75.7.3034); primary scanned theorem page saved |
    54	| LAD, i.i.d. median-zero errors with continuous positive density near zero | With V_n^2=S_n>0 and max_i ||V_n^(-1)x_i||->0, 2f(0)V_n(T_n-beta_0) converges to N(0,I); this implies weak consistency for nested rows | [Pollard (1991), Theorem 1, p. 189](https://doi.org/10.1017/S0266466600004394); author PDF and four page renders saved |
